architecture store-schema-registry
  source_lineage earliest source .githooks/pre-commit first committed 2026-08-15 in 1c82a929 "feat(activation+auto): close the opportunity family; make the atlas auto-used"
  canonical_name StoreSchemaRegistry
  family storage
  domain Storage / Native Store DDL
  layer substrate
  semantic_question Which tables, indexes, views and triggers does each native owner create in its SQLite store, declared once rather than hand-written as C string literals in every owner?
  purpose Holds every native owner's store DDL in schemas/storage/stores (one CUE file per owner, statements tagged kind and name); scripts/compile-store-schemas.sh compiles each owner's fragments to <owner>/generated/store_schema.h as string macros that the owner's init passes to SQLite unchanged.
  maturity implemented
  source_path schemas/storage/stores/store.cue
  source_path scripts/compile-store-schemas.sh
  source_path .githooks/pre-commit
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/include/bf_store_durability.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/tests/store_durability_test.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreVec/tests/vector_store_kind_test.c
  source_path schemas/storage/stores/cmd-BonfyreWebAddress.cue
  source_path schemas/storage/stores/cmd-BonfyreConnectionCatalog.cue
  source_path schemas/storage/stores/cmd-BonfyreSurfaceMaturity.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/web_store.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreBitNet/tests/ranker_store_kind_test.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/dynamic_store_kind_test.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreConnectionCatalog/tests/catalog_test.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSpatial/tests/spatial_test.sh
  source_path scripts/ui-ratchet.sh
  invariant each fragment is byte-for-byte the literal the owner executed before, so stores created before and after the move have identical sqlite_master text; the move changes where the text lives, not what SQLite sees
  invariant joined in order, a fragment's statements are the fragment; kind and name are read from each statement and a table, index, view or trigger row must start with the matching CREATE clause
  invariant a generated header is never edited by hand; compile-store-schemas.sh --check refuses a header that differs from the registry, and the pre-commit hook runs it
  invariant the ui-ratchet handwritten_ddl count of CREATE TABLE in cmd/*/src and components/*/src C and H sources may only go down
  invariant a declared store names its kind (sqlite, vector, ranker, columnar, dynamic) and the compiler emits BF_STORE_<macro>_KIND plus that kind's shape constants: vector table, width or runtime, metric, quantization, model; ranker key space, run and frontier tables, key and order columns, weights passport and the generated frontier order query; columnar format, cold location, declared columns, a bound cold scan, a missing-columns check over parquet_schema, and for a hot shadow its DuckDB attach, ordered export and (ddl columns) hot DDL, plus the promotion rule; dynamic shard, and for shard named a BfStoreJoin array (schema name, env, probe table, required) with the bound ATTACH ?1 AS ?2; every owner in opened_by gets the same constants
  invariant a store declares durability (writer policy) or lease (reader busy timeout and read deadline), never both; either compiles to a static bf_store_policy_<name> in the owner's header
  invariant every store file a WebAddress serve worker opens goes through bf_store_open, bf_store_open_ro or cms_open_ro/rw with its declared policy; the ui-ratchet direct_store_opens count (raw sqlite3_open*/bf_sqlite_open_readonly_path in WebAddress src, private :memory: databases excepted) is 0 and may only stay there
  invariant bf_store_open applies a declared writer policy only on a read-write open of a store that declares durability; a lease-only store opened read-write keeps its writer's pragmas
  invariant lease state is one process-wide table shared by every translation unit (weak definitions), so a connection opened in site_mcp.c or detail_depth.c is reaped by the serve loop in main.c; a leak report names the opening file:line
  invariant a process-lifetime handle (the receipt pack) is opened with bf_store_open_held: declared busy timeout, never leased, so the end of a request cannot close it
  invariant a store with durability compiles to one BfStoreDurability initializer; every writer of the CMS store (bonfyre-cms and WebAddress cms_open_rw) applies it through bf_store_writer, and every WebAddress cms_open_ro/rw connection is leased to the request that opened it
  invariant a writer commit that leaves the WAL at or past wal_truncate_pages runs a TRUNCATE checkpoint; after a refusal it waits another wal_truncate_pages before retrying, so a long reader costs writers one wait per threshold
  invariant at the end of every served request, connections the request left open are finalized and closed and reported on stderr; a request that holds a leased store past read_txn_max_ms is ended by SIGALRM (worker exits 75 and the pool restarts)
  invariant the ui-ratchet handwritten_store_shapes count (CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE, USING vec0, "ATTACH, read_parquet( in C sources) may only go down
  forbidden_inference a declared durability policy -> the WAL is bounded; a reader blocked outside SQLite inside the deadline, or an owner that opens the file without the policy, still pins it
  forbidden_inference a vector store declared -> its embeddings are current, were made by the named model, or that sqlite-vec is loadable where the owner runs
  forbidden_inference a ranker store declared -> its order is relevant, admitted or better than the deterministic frontier; the kind names where the learned order lives, the passport decides what it may be used for
  forbidden_inference a columnar store whose files carry the declared columns -> their rows are correct, current or complete; the check is names only, not types or content
  forbidden_inference a dynamic join that attached -> the joined store is fresh or that the request may read every row in it; the probe proves one table exists
  forbidden_inference a lease-only declaration -> WebAddress governs that store's journal; the writer owns its policy
  forbidden_inference a declared table -> the owner's store exists, is migrated, holds data, or that any other owner may read or write it; the registry names DDL, not access rights or a migration plan
  witness scripts/compile-store-schemas.sh --check; a compiled probe prints every macro and matches the 219 literals captured from the hand-written sources byte for byte; Auth, Finance, Entity and Space stores created by the old and new binaries have identical .schema output; owner test suites pass
  witness make -C cmd/BonfyreCMS store-durability-test: under the declared CMS policy with a reader process that always holds a read transaction, a passive-only writer's WAL reaches 460 MB while the declared writer stays at 67.5 MB (bound 67.7 MB, 6 truncations); a leaked statement pins the WAL to 231 MB until bf_store_leases_end reaps it, then the WAL falls back under the bound; a request blocked past read_txn_max_ms exits 75
  witness make -C cmd/BonfyreVec vector-store-kind-test: vec_artifacts built from BF_STORE_VEC_INDEX_VECTOR_DDL at width 4 holds exactly the registry text in sqlite_master and sqlite-vec answers the nearest neighbours a, c
  witness WebAddress serving preview copies across ~1900 GET requests (HTML, JSON, signed-in) reaped no leased CMS connection
  witness make -C cmd/BonfyreBitNet ranker-store-kind-test: a rank store built from the bitnet_rank_run fragment, attached read-only by BF_STORE_BITNET_RANK_ATTACH, returns its frontier through BF_STORE_BITNET_RANK_RANKER_FRONTIER in rank order and refuses a write; contract_test.sh evaluate-retention passes through the same attach
  witness sh cmd/BonfyreConnectionCatalog/tests/catalog_test.sh: a facets file lacking catalogue is refused by the declared missing-columns check; the real 7,106-row connector-facets and 10,052-row source-entries Parquet files read back through the declared schema
  witness sh cmd/BonfyreSpatial/tests/spatial_test.sh: the exported cold Parquet carries all 19 declared spatial_fact_cold columns and hot/cold fidelity is identical
  witness make -C cmd/BonfyreWebAddress dynamic-store-kind-test: item_depth joins by its declared rows; a present store with its probe joins, an absent store and one without its probe table do not; joined stores refuse writes
  witness 2026-11-15 tree vs HEAD WebAddress binaries on separate preview lanes, 376 requests (188 routes x HTML/JSON): identical status and Location everywhere; bodies identical except routes-agent 404 pages, asset version hashes, nonces and the capability listing order of the archived tree; zero leases reaped, no deadline exits
  known_gap the 13 GB CMS WAL of 2026-11-15 was written by the release activity-public-20261021, whose bonfyre-web-address and bonfyre-cms carry no wal_autocheckpoint, journal_size_limit or TRUNCATE policy at all; the leak or long reader in that build was not identified, and the fix takes effect only once a release built from this tree is installed
  known_gap most stores WebAddress opens are declared under cmd/BonfyreWebAddress with written_by naming the real owner; they move to their owners' files (WebAddress joining opened_by) as those owners declare them
  known_gap handwritten_store_shapes keeps 2: BonfyreBridge composes DuckDB ATTACH for endpoints named at run time, and BonfyreCanon's classifier matches the text "ATTACH " in literals it reads; neither is a store shape
  known_gap the CMS store-durability witness's bounded-WAL step is timing-sensitive under machine load (1 of 5 runs refused one TRUNCATE with both the HEAD and the tree header)
  known_gap the tenant and site shards of the dynamic kind compile but no owner uses them; the owners moved are named joins
  known_gap DDL composed with C macros (cmd/BonfyreCMS account_world_literature, account_world_music, account_world_audio) and DDL built at run time with format arguments (BonfyreBridge) are still in source; ALTER TABLE migrations and columns added after creation live in owner code, not here; BitNet, ConnectionCatalog, SurfaceMaturity and WebAddress's dynamic witness now list generated/store_schema.h as a prerequisite; other owners' Makefiles do not yet

interaction store-durability-binds-cms-writers
  source store-schema-registry
  destination cmd-c-m-s
  relation compiled-journal-policy
  preserves journal mode, synchronous, autocheckpoint pages, journal_size_limit, truncate threshold, busy timeout and read deadline exactly as declared for store cms
  drops any claim that the store's contents, migrations or access rights are governed by the policy
  forbidden_inference the policy is applied -> no reader can pin the WAL
  binding cmd/BonfyreCMS/src/main.c bf_store_writer(g_db, &cms_store_durability)
  witness make -C cmd/BonfyreCMS store-durability-test

interaction store-durability-leases-web-readers
  source store-schema-registry
  destination cmd-web-address
  relation request-scoped-store-lease
  preserves one connection lifetime per request for every declared store a worker opens (CMS and the lease-only stores); leaked connections closed at request end; requests past read_txn_max_ms ended
  drops which owner leaked, beyond the opening file:line (or caller address) printed on stderr
  forbidden_inference zero reaped leases in a crawl -> no route leaks; only the routes asked were observed
  binding cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/world_federation_and_protocols.h cms_open_ro/cms_open_rw; bf_store_open/bf_store_open_ro at every WebAddress open (web_store.h); cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c bf_store_leases_end after bf_web_route_dispatch
  witness WebAddress gate tests and a preview-copy crawl with leak reports counted

interaction vector-kind-compiles-vec-index
  source store-schema-registry
  destination cmd-vec
  relation vector-store-ddl
  preserves table name, runtime width passed by the owner, l2 metric, float32 elements
  drops the embed model's identity; the model string is a description, not a passport check
  forbidden_inference a vector store declared -> its embeddings are current
  binding cmd/BonfyreVec/src/main.c and cmd/BonfyreEmbed/src/main.c format BF_STORE_*_INDEX_VECTOR_DDL with their width
  witness make -C cmd/BonfyreVec vector-store-kind-test

interaction ranker-kind-binds-bitnet-rank-store
  source store-schema-registry
  destination cmd-bit-net
  relation ranker-store-attach-and-frontier
  preserves run and frontier tables, key and order columns, read-only attach as rank_source, rank order of the frontier
  drops the representation passport's standing; the weights string names the passport, it does not check it
  forbidden_inference a ranker store declared -> its rank is relevance, selection or admission
  binding cmd/BonfyreBitNet/src/main.c evaluate_retention bf_store_attach(BF_STORE_BITNET_RANK_ATTACH) and BF_STORE_BITNET_RANK_RANKER_FRONTIER
  witness make -C cmd/BonfyreBitNet ranker-store-kind-test

interaction columnar-kind-binds-spatial-durable-tier
  source store-schema-registry
  destination cmd-spatial
  relation columnar-hot-shadow-export
  preserves hot table spatial_fact as source, DuckDB read-only hot attach, export ordered by fact_id with zstd, cold scan for verify, thaw-only promotion
  drops columns added later by ALTER TABLE from the declared promise (they still ride along in the export)
  forbidden_inference a cold file with the declared columns -> it may replace the hot store; only --verify identical says the same facts
  binding cmd/BonfyreSpatial/src/main.c cmd_durable BF_STORE_SPATIAL_FACT_COLD_COLUMNAR_*; plane attach BF_STORE_SPATIAL_ADDRESS_PLANE_ATTACH
  witness sh cmd/BonfyreSpatial/tests/spatial_test.sh

interaction columnar-kind-binds-connection-catalog
  source store-schema-registry
  destination cmd-web-address
  relation columnar-cold-only-read
  preserves the declared facets and entries columns, bound cold scans, refusal of a file lacking a declared column
  drops any hot shadow; the catalogue keeps none
  forbidden_inference the catalogue files carry the declared columns -> their candidates are verified sources
  binding cmd/BonfyreConnectionCatalog/src/main.c declared_columns and BF_STORE_CONNECTION_*_COLUMNAR_COLD_SCAN_BOUND (the catalogue serves WebAddress connection pages)
  witness sh cmd/BonfyreConnectionCatalog/tests/catalog_test.sh

interaction dynamic-kind-binds-detail-depth
  source store-schema-registry
  destination detail-depth
  relation named-store-joins
  preserves schema names fr, fp, dd, jt, their environment variables and probe tables; read-only URI attaches bound as ?1/?2
  drops freshness of the joined stores
  forbidden_inference a join attached -> the item page may show every row of the joined store
  binding cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/detail_depth.c sess_open and bf_detail_depth_measure through bf_store_join(item_depth_joins)
  witness make -C cmd/BonfyreWebAddress dynamic-store-kind-test; BONFYRE_TEST_WEB_BINARY=... sh cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/detail_depth_test.sh

interaction dynamic-kind-binds-surface-maturity
  source store-schema-registry
  destination cmd-surface-maturity
  relation named-store-joins
  preserves the seven estate joins (cms required) attached read-only under their declared names
  drops which estate directory names each file; the owner resolves paths
  forbidden_inference every join attached -> the estate is mature; the audit gates decide that
  binding cmd/BonfyreSurfaceMaturity/src/main.c load_estate attach_db through bf_store_join(estate_joins)
  witness sh cmd/BonfyreSurfaceMaturity/tests/surface_maturity_test.sh
